 735:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****  [..]
 736:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the SPI
 737:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****     data transfers.
 738:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 739:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****     [..] The SPI supports master and slave mode :
 740:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 741:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****     (#) There are two modes of transfer:
 742:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****        (++) Blocking mode: The communication is performed in polling mode.
 743:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****             The HAL status of all data processing is returned by the same function
 744:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****             after finishing transfer.
 745:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****        (++) No-Blocking mode: The communication is performed using Interrupts
 746:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****             or DMA, These APIs return the HAL status.
 747:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****             The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
 748:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****             dedicated SPI IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when
 749:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****             using DMA mode.
 750:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****             The HAL_SPI_TxCpltCallback(), HAL_SPI_RxCpltCallback() and HAL_SPI_TxRxCpltCallback() u
 751:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****             will be executed respectively at the end of the transmit or Receive process
 752:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****             The HAL_SPI_ErrorCallback()user callback will be executed when a communication error is
 753:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c **** 
 754:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****     (#) APIs provided for these 2 transfer modes (Blocking mode or Non blocking mode using either I
 755:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c ****         exist for 1Line (simplex) and 2Lines (full duplex) modes.
 756:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_spi.c **** 
